&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vos missions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Au sein de l&#39;équipe Public Affairs de Doctolib, vous jouez un rôle stratégique au cœur de l&#39;écosystème de santé français. Rattaché(e) au responsable du pôle Santé, vous êtes l&#39;interlocuteur(rice) de référence de Doctolib auprès des syndicats professionnels, ordres médicaux et paramédicaux ainsi que des associations de patients. Vous garantissez un déploiement fluide et durable de nos produits sur le marché, tout en servant de point d&#39;écoute privilégié pour améliorer en continu nos solutions et notre go-to-market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vos responsabilités incluent, mais ne sont pas limitées à :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Construire, animer et coordonner les relations avec les KOLs, syndicats professionnels, ordres médicaux et paramédicaux, CPAM et URPS : suivi régulier, partage de messages, représentation de Doctolib lors des instances clés&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sécuriser le déploiement des produits de Doctolib en suivant les négociations conventionnelles, les sujets de remboursement et de subventionnement numérique, en lien avec les équipes internes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Développer et structurer des partenariats avec les associations de patients et assurer la coordination locale des représentations médicales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Être le relais terrain vers les équipes Produit et Marketing : remontée des retours utilisateurs, contribution aux argumentaires produit, suivi des lancements et des sujets de conventionnement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Piloter la stratégie de contenu des fiches médecins en lien avec le Customer Care, en assurant une gestion fluide des frictions et une capacité à négocier les désaccords&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborer étroitement avec les équipes internes (Produit, Customer Care, Marketing) pour anticiper les sujets à risque, contribuer à la limitation des crises et garantir un go-to-market sans friction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Les qualités attendues en tant que Responsable Partenaires Écosystème Santé&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Avant de poursuivre votre lecture, si vous n&#39;avez pas le profil exact décrit ci-dessous, mais que vous pensez que cette description de poste correspond à vos compétences et à vos aspirations, nous vous encourageons tout de même à postuler.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vous pourrez être le prochain membre de notre équipe si vous :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Avez une connaissance intime du milieu médical et paramédical : son fonctionnement, ses codes et ses acteurs (syndicats, ordres, instances représentatives)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maîtrisez les enjeux de partenariats et de relations institutionnelles dans le secteur de la santé, et savez naviguer dans des environnements politiquement complexes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Êtes reconnu(e) pour votre capacité d&#39;écoute active, votre sens du collectif et votre aptitude à faire remonter des informations terrain de manière structurée et actionnable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Savez créer des relations de confiance durables avec des interlocuteurs exigeants, et êtes capable de négocier avec diplomatie tout en défendant les intérêts de Doctolib&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travaillez en forte collaboration avec des équipes internes pluridisciplinaires (Produit, Marketing, Customer Care) et savez aligner les parties prenantes autour d&#39;objectifs communs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ce serait fantastique si :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vous avez une expérience dans un syndicat de médecins, une institution professionnelle de santé ou une organisation représentative du secteur&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vous avez une connaissance des sujets de remboursement, conventionnement ou subventionnement numérique dans le domaine de la santé&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vous avez évolué dans un environnement medtech ou healthtech avec une forte exposition aux professionnels de santé&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Notre offre&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une mutuelle avantageuse prise en charge à 100 % par Doctolib (régime de base) pour les employés et leurs enfants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 jours de congés payés et 12 à 14 jours de RTT par an&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un programme de santé mentale et de coaching personnalisé gratuit avec notre partenaire Moka.care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10 jours par an de télétravail à l&#39;étranger possible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Des tickets restaurant d&#39;une valeur de 8,50 € par jour, dont 4,50 € pris en charge par Doctolib&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adhésion au plan de partage de la valeur de Doctolib, appelé DoctoGrowth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un programme d&#39;intégration complet de 3 mois incluant la Doctolib Academy et diverses formations (langues, soft skills, compétences techniques)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une subvention du comité d&#39;entreprise pour le remboursement partiel d&#39;adhésions à des activités sportives ou de loisirs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un remboursement à 50 % de l&#39;abonnement aux transports en commun&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Programme ParentCare : bénéficiez d&#39;un congé de naissance couvert par Doctolib à 100 % le premier mois et à 75 % le deuxième mois&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pour les salariés en situation de handicap ou proches aidants, un package comprenant une adaptation du télétravail, des jours d&#39;absence autorisée payés pour les rendez-vous médicaux et un soutien psychologique renforcé&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Aide au déménagement en cas de mobilité internationale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Le processus de recrutement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Entretien avec un(e) recruteur(se)&lt;/strong&gt; (30 min, en ligne)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rencontre avec le/la Hiring Manager&lt;/strong&gt; (1h, en ligne)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Entretien technique et mise en situation&lt;/strong&gt; (1h, en présentiel)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prise de références&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Détails du poste&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CDI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Temps plein&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Levallois-Perret&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prise de poste : ASAP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybride (2 jours de télétravail par semaine)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Chez Doctolib, nous sommes convaincus que nous devons améliorer la santé pour tout le monde. Cela se reflète dans notre processus de recrutement. Nous évaluons les candidatures uniquement sur la base des qualifications et de la motivation, sans aucune forme de discrimination.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Plus les idées sont diverses, plus notre produit améliorera véritablement la santé pour tout le monde. Vous pouvez postuler chez Doctolib, quel que soit votre genre, religion, âge, orientation sexuelle, origine ethnique ou handicap.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Afin de garantir l&#39;égalité des chances, nous vous invitons à exclure les informations personnelles (par exemple : photos, âge) de vos candidatures. Si vous avez besoin d&#39;aménagements particuliers, merci de nous en informer pour que nous puissions adapter le processus de recrutement. Rejoignez-nous pour construire la santé dont nous rêvons tous !&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Toutes les informations fournies sont traitées par Doctolib pour la gestion des candidatures. Pour plus de détails sur le traitement des données, cliquez&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://doctolib.legal/B2C-Privacy-Policy-Career-FR&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;ici&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;. Veuillez contacter ----- pour toute question ou pour exercer vos droits.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Now is an amazing time to join Nozomi Networks as we build the future of OT and IoT cybersecurity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We defend some of the world’s largest organizations and critical infrastructure in more than 68 countries and we’re just getting started. Our AI-powered cybersecurity platform secures operational technology (OT) and Internet of Things (IoT) infrastructures for enterprises and government entities across energy, manufacturing, transportation, resources, and critical infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Nozomi Networks is seeking an experienced, highly technical Senior Salesforce (SFDC) Developer to design, build, integrate, and support enterprise solutions across the Salesforce ecosystem. This is a hands-on engineering role for a developer with deep Salesforce expertise who can personally solve complex technical problems across Apex, Lightning Web Components, APIs, integrations, automation, data, security, Slack, and emerging AI technologies.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:80,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:247}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The ideal candidate is a builder, not simply a Salesforce administrator or configuration specialist. This individual will translate complex business requirements into scalable technical solutions, write production-quality code, troubleshoot difficult issues, integrate Salesforce with enterprise platforms, and own solutions from architecture through deployment and production support.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:80,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:247}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;A major focus of the role will be advancing Nozomi Networks&#39; use of modern AI and agentic technologies, including Salesforce Agentforce, Salesforce AI capabilities, generative AI, Slack-based experiences, and AI-driven workflow automation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:80,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:247}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, develop, test, deploy, and maintain scalable solutions across Salesforce using Apex, Lightning Web Components, Flow, SOQL/SOSL, Platform Events, and related technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build AI-enabled solutions using Salesforce Agentforce, generative AI, LLM APIs, RAG, Prompt Builder, and intelligent automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop Salesforce and Slack integrations, applications, bots, workflows, and AI-powered employee experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design secure and reliable integrations between Salesforce and enterprise systems using REST/SOAP APIs, OAuth, webhooks, middleware, and event-driven architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with GTM Architecture, Security, Data, Infrastructure, and other teams to align solutions with business processes and enterprise standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply modern software engineering practices, including Git, Salesforce DX/CLI, CI/CD, automated testing, code reviews, monitoring, and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot complex production issues and continuously improve application performance, security, scalability, and maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To be successful in this opportunity, you will have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of Salesforce platform experience with significant hands-on development responsibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced experience with Apex, Lightning Web Components, SOQL, Salesforce data modeling, Flow, and automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience designing REST APIs, enterprise integrations, and secure Salesforce solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Git-based development, CI/CD, automated testing, debugging, and production support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience developing AI-enabled applications using technologies such as Agentforce, generative AI, LLMs, RAG, AI agents, or semantic search.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to translate complex technical and business requirements into secure, scalable production solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent technical documentation, troubleshooting, and communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Slack development and integration, including APIs, applications, bots, workflows, OAuth, Events API, and webhooks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salesforce Sales Cloud, Service Cloud, Experience Cloud, Data Cloud, and Agentforce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MuleSoft or comparable integration platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AWS, Azure, or comparable cloud services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enterprise API architecture, identity and access management, and modern data platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience within a SaaS, cybersecurity, or fast-growing global technology organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant Salesforce certifications, including Platform Developer I/II or architecture-focused credentials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are and what we stand for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nozomi Networks is the leader in OT and IoT Cybersecurity. We protect the world&#39;s critical infrastructure, industrial and government organizations from cyber threats by providing exceptional network visibility, threat detection and operational insight. We’re always innovating and we hire the best at what they do to ensure our customers always have access to fast product enhancements, exceptional engineering support and rapid deployment across continents.&amp;nbsp;If you like a challenge, and value integrity and customer success, we invite you to help Nozomi Networks build the future of OT and IoT cybersecurity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging are part of our core beliefs, at Nozomi Networks. Diversity of thought, background and culture broadens our knowledge of the world and helps us learn, grow, and gain new perspectives. What makes us all different is what makes us powerful.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Global Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All of our benefits are customized to the country you are based in, naturally we want to get the best out of our Nozomiers, so we provide the best benefits packages, such as:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health &amp;amp; Wellness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Financial&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work-Life Balance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unparalleled Flexible Time-Off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Need to know information&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Successful candidates will be subjected to background verification checks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Be cautious of unsolicited messages, fake email addresses, requests for money and unclear job descriptions. Report suspicious activity to authorities. Our open job opportunities and descriptions are posted on Nozomi Networks&#39; career page. If in any doubt please apply for opportunities on our careers website &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nozominetworks.com/company/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you would like to know more about our Privacy Policy, please click &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nozominetworks.com/legal/job-applicant-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. Any questions about how we process personal information, or if you would like help exercising your privacy rights please contact us using the email provided within the Privacy Policy.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Customer Success Architect, you&#39;ll serve as a trusted strategic advisor and technical authority to some of GitLab&#39;s most complex and high-value Enterprise and Government customers across Japan. In this role, you will be driving and shaping how our largest customers adopt GitLab&#39;s intelligent DevSecOps platform to achieve their business goals and realise meaningful, long-term outcomes. You will be working closely with customers after the sale to turn pre-sales command plans into clear success plans, guide them through their customer journey, and drive adoption, utilization, and technical maturity. You will also be directly influencing renewal and expansion decisions through your post-sales engagements with executive-level decision makers in the account.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a individual-contributor role for someone who has already led pre or post sales customer engagements in large complex accounts across multiple industry domains to drive quantifiable business outcomes..The individual is comfortable operating with&amp;nbsp; ambiguity, and can credibly advise VP- and C-level stakeholders on business transformation, application modernization, platform strategy, architecture, and organizational DevSecOps transformation. You&#39;ll also be shaping playbooks and best practices, and acting as an escalation point for the team&#39;s most technically or politically complex situations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting into the APJ Customer Success organization, you&#39;ll own a portfolio of GitLab&#39;s most strategic enterprise and Government accounts, act as the executive-level technical liaison for these accounts, and drive cross-functional resolution of their highest-priority issues — coordinating and, where needed, directing the efforts of Product Management, Engineering, Sales, Professional Services, and Support. You&#39;ll bring deep technical expertise in CI/CD, cloud platforms, multi-cloud, hybrid architecture and enterprise DevSecOps practices.You will use that expertise to shape customers&#39; long-term platform strategy, apply best practices, configure GitLab for their environments and stay current with platform capabilities. In your first year, success will look like establishing yourself as the trusted senior advisor across a portfolio of flagship accounts, building strong relationships with key stakeholders, materially improving and increasing platform maturity, leading retention and renewal conversations, increasing customer satisfaction across your portfolio and contributing to the broader CSA team&#39;s technical standards and ways of working.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Some examples of our projects:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turning pre-sales command plans into measurable customer success plans that align technical adoption with business outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading and driving the technical strategy behind a large-scale DevSecOps platform consolidation for a regulated Enterprise account or Government, including guiding enterprise customers on GitLab best practices across CI/CD, DevSecOps, cloud architecture, TCO, applying compliance and architecture as well as business case presentations to customer executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning end-to-end resolution of a critical, multi-team escalation for a flagship account — driving root cause analysis, coordinating Engineering/Product/Support, and personally briefing customer executives on remediation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owns a book of Enterprise and Government customers and drive adoption, retention, expansion, and overall satisfaction through ongoing strategic, business and technical engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serves as the senior post-sales strategic, business and technical advisor for a portfolio of GitLab&#39;s most complex, highest-value enterprise and Government accounts, shaping multi-year platform and DevSecOps strategy in partnership with customer executives, coordinating responses to questions, issues, and escalations across Support, Product Management, Sales, and Professional Services. &lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translates ambiguous, high-stakes business outcomes into rigorous Customer Success Plans that are regularly reviewed with customer stakeholders. The Customer Success Plans contain clearly defined business outcome related goals, quantifiable benefits, realistic adoption milestones and remediation actions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepares executive-ready reporting conducted on a regular basis with clear accountability for outcomes that demonstrate impact on adoption, retention, and expansion of GitLab products and services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provides deep technical guidance on enterprise-scale CI/CD architecture, DevSecOps maturity models, platform consolidation strategy, including advising on complex trade-offs (e.g., multi-cloud vs. hybrid, self-managed vs. GitLab Dedicated, etc).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owns the full lifecycle of your account portfolio&#39;s adoption, retention, and expansion outcomes, with direct accountability for the commercial and technical health of flagship relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leads end-to-end resolution of critical, cross-functional account escalations, ensuring root causes are identified, follow-up actions are owned, holding internal teams accountable to timelines, driving the root cause analysis and personally managing executive communication and risk.&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leads end-to-end resolution of critical, cross-functional account escalations, ensuring &amp;nbsp; root causes are identified, follow-up actions are owned, holding internal teams accountable to timelines, driving the driving root cause analysis and personally managing executive communication and risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designs and delivers technical enablement programs at scale, identifying systemic maturity gaps across a portfolio and building the roadmap (not just individual sessions) that closes them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advises key customers stakeholders on cloud and platform architecture decisions with enterprise-wide impact, which includes&amp;nbsp; multi-region deployment strategy, secrets management architecture and network/security topology for regulated environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guides customers on GitLab platform best practices including Git workflows, branching strategies, CI/CD pipeline design, DevSecOps adoption patterns, and security scanning configuration.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provides hands-on technical enablement and onboarding, including education on GitLab features, releases, and use cases, and identification of training and maturity opportunities aligned to customer goals.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engages customers on cloud platform architecture decisions relevant to their GitLab deployment — including self-managed vs. GitLab Dedicated, Runner configuration and auto-scaling, secrets management, and network topology considerations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advises customers on DevSecOps consolidation value — articulating the TCO, compliance, and developer experience case for platform consolidation over fragmented toolchains.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborates with Professional Services, Sales, and internal teams to identify expansion opportunities, recommend enablement interventions, and ensure a seamless customer journey from onboarding through renewal.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be a Japanese citizen based in Japan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mandatory Japanese (native or professional level) and English language proficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building or owning CI/CD pipelines end to end, including pipeline as code, multi-stage design, artifact management, and troubleshooting in real-world environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A career built across different direct customer facing engagement roles such as Technical Account Management, Technical Solution Sales, Pre-sales, Business Development, Consulting, Professional services across customers in different industry vertical domains like Government, Banking, Financial and Insurance Services, Manufacturing, Telecommunications, engagement with multiple technology and platform transition experience such as from on-premise deployments to Cloud, application modernization experience from monolith to microservices, from Waterfall to DevOps to DevSecOps and others to provide the depth and breadth of experience to advise customers on transformations and deployments that you&#39;ve already seen play out elsewhere across your multiple customer engagements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A long-standing demonstrated track record as the person other senior people call when an account is in genuine crisis or gained across a sustained career of Enterprise or Government account ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Credible judgment earned by personally owning the outcomes of dozens of complex enterprise customer account engagements over the course of a career, including situations with real commercial, technical, and reputational stakes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A consistent track record of being trusted by customer executives and internal leadership to operate with minimal oversight in ambiguous and high-pressure situations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep, hands-on expertise in DevSecOps practices, including shift-left security and integrating SAST, DAST, SCA, and container scanning into development workflows as well as architecting and troubleshooting CI/CD pipelines at enterprise scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level understanding of Git, merge request workflows and delivery lifecycles, having personally guided organizations through branching strategies such as trunk-based development and GitFlow, and modern software delivery lifecycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience with infrastructure as code, GitOps, Cloud and on-premises environments with relevant experience that support GitLab deployments, including networking, identity and access management (IAM), secrets management, and deployment considerations for regulated or high-security environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience partnering with customers to turn business requirements into actionable success plans, with measurable goals and verifiable business outcomes that are suitable for executive-level quarterly reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to drive product adoption, dive deep into the accounts assigned and scale out the level of influence in the account.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build and defend executive-level business cases (TCO, compliance, risk) that influence budget and platform strategy decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to operate with autonomy in ambiguous, high-stakes situations with strong communication, stakeholder management, and organizational experience&amp;nbsp; to manage a portfolio of enterprise and Government customers, balance multiple priorities, guide escalations, and coordinate effectively across customer teams and internal cross functional teams to resolve issues appropriately and in a timely manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Customer Success Architect team is part of GitLab&#39;s Customer Experience organization. It supports strategic enterprise and Government accounts across the APJ region through hands-on technical guidance, consultative partnership, and practical problem solving.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We act as a reliable technical advisor and an important link between customers and the broader GitLab ecosystem. We bring platform, cloud, and DevSecOps depth to customer engagements and work closely with Product Management, Engineering, Sales, Support, and Professional Services to address questions, guide customers through technical choices, navigate escalations, and help them realize measurable value from GitLab.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Composed of team members working remotely across time zones, we operate asynchronously to support a focused set of strategic accounts across the region. It&#39;s a team well suited for people who enjoy solving complex customer challenges, building long-term partnerships, and helping enterprise organizations grow their maturity with GitLab in practical, measurable ways.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Customer Success Architect, you&#39;ll serve as a trusted strategic advisor and technical authority to some of GitLab&#39;s most complex and high-value Enterprise and Government customers across Singapore. In this role, you will be driving and shaping how our largest customers adopt GitLab&#39;s intelligent DevSecOps platform to achieve their business goals and realise meaningful, long-term outcomes. You will be working closely with customers after the sale to turn pre-sales command plans into clear success plans, guide them through their customer journey, and drive adoption, utilization, and technical maturity. You will also be directly influencing renewal and expansion decisions through your post-sales engagements with executive-level decision makers in the account.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior individual-contributor role for someone who has already led high-stakes pre or post sales customer engagements in large complex accounts across multiple industry domains to drive quantifiable business outcomes..The individual is comfortable operating with&amp;nbsp; ambiguity, and can credibly advise VP- and C-level stakeholders on business transformation, application modernization, platform strategy, architecture, and organizational DevSecOps transformation. You&#39;ll also be shaping playbooks and best practices, and acting as an escalation point for the team&#39;s most technically or politically complex situations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting into the APJ Customer Success organization, you&#39;ll own a portfolio of GitLab&#39;s most strategic enterprise and Government accounts, act as the executive-level technical liaison for these accounts, and drive cross-functional resolution of their highest-priority issues — coordinating and, where needed, directing the efforts of Product Management, Engineering, Sales, Professional Services, and Support. You&#39;ll bring deep technical expertise in CI/CD, cloud platforms, multi-cloud, hybrid architecture and enterprise DevSecOps practices.You will use that expertise to shape customers&#39; long-term platform strategy, apply best practices, configure GitLab for their environments and stay current with platform capabilities. In your first year, success will look like establishing yourself as the trusted senior advisor across a portfolio of flagship accounts, building strong relationships with key stakeholders, materially improving and increasing platform maturity, leading retention and renewal conversations, increasing customer satisfaction across your portfolio and contributing to the broader CSA team&#39;s technical standards and ways of working.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Some examples of our projects:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turning pre-sales command plans into measurable customer success plans that align technical adoption with business outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading and driving the technical strategy behind a large-scale DevSecOps platform consolidation for a regulated Enterprise account or Government, including guiding enterprise customers on GitLab best practices across CI/CD, DevSecOps, cloud architecture, TCO, applying compliance and architecture as well as business case presentations to customer executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning end-to-end resolution of a critical, multi-team escalation for a flagship account — driving root cause analysis, coordinating Engineering/Product/Support, and personally briefing customer executives on remediation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owns a book of Enterprise and Government customers and drive adoption, retention, expansion, and overall satisfaction through ongoing strategic, business and technical engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serves as the senior post-sales strategic, business and technical advisor for a portfolio of GitLab&#39;s most complex, highest-value enterprise and Government accounts, shaping multi-year platform and DevSecOps strategy in partnership with customer executives, coordinating responses to questions, issues, and escalations across Support, Product Management, Sales, and Professional Services. &lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translates ambiguous, high-stakes business outcomes into rigorous Customer Success Plans that are regularly reviewed with customer stakeholders. The Customer Success Plans contain clearly defined business outcome related goals, quantifiable benefits, realistic adoption milestones and remediation actions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepares executive-ready reporting conducted on a regular basis with clear accountability for outcomes that demonstrate impact on adoption, retention, and expansion of GitLab products and services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provides deep technical guidance on enterprise-scale CI/CD architecture, DevSecOps maturity models, platform consolidation strategy, including advising on complex trade-offs (e.g., multi-cloud vs. hybrid, self-managed vs. GitLab Dedicated, etc).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owns the full lifecycle of your account portfolio&#39;s adoption, retention, and expansion outcomes, with direct accountability for the commercial and technical health of flagship relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leads end-to-end resolution of critical, cross-functional account escalations, ensuring root causes are identified, follow-up actions are owned, holding internal teams accountable to timelines, driving the root cause analysis and personally managing executive communication and risk.&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leads end-to-end resolution of critical, cross-functional account escalations, ensuring &amp;nbsp; root causes are identified, follow-up actions are owned, holding internal teams accountable to timelines, driving the driving root cause analysis and personally managing executive communication and risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designs and delivers technical enablement programs at scale, identifying systemic maturity gaps across a portfolio and building the roadmap (not just individual sessions) that closes them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advises key customers stakeholders on cloud and platform architecture decisions with enterprise-wide impact, which includes&amp;nbsp; multi-region deployment strategy, secrets management architecture and network/security topology for regulated environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guides customers on GitLab platform best practices including Git workflows, branching strategies, CI/CD pipeline design, DevSecOps adoption patterns, and security scanning configuration.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provides hands-on technical enablement and onboarding, including education on GitLab features, releases, and use cases, and identification of training and maturity opportunities aligned to customer goals.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engages customers on cloud platform architecture decisions relevant to their GitLab deployment — including self-managed vs. GitLab Dedicated, Runner configuration and auto-scaling, secrets management, and network topology considerations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advises customers on DevSecOps consolidation value — articulating the TCO, compliance, and developer experience case for platform consolidation over fragmented toolchains.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborates with Professional Services, Sales, and internal teams to identify expansion opportunities, recommend enablement interventions, and ensure a seamless customer journey from onboarding through renewal.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be a Singapore Citizen and based in Singapore&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mandatory English language proficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building or owning CI/CD pipelines end to end, including pipeline as code, multi-stage design, artifact management, and troubleshooting in real-world environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A career built across different direct customer facing engagement roles such as Technical Account Management, Technical Solution Sales, Pre-sales, Business Development, Consulting, Professional services across customers in different industry vertical domains like Government, Banking, Financial and Insurance Services, Manufacturing, Telecommunications, engagement with multiple technology and platform transition experience such as from on-premise deployments to Cloud, application modernization experience from monolith to microservices,&amp;nbsp; from Waterfall to DevOps to DevSecOps and others to provide the depth and breadth of experience to advise customers on transformations and deployments that you&#39;ve already seen play out elsewhere across your multiple customer engagements, more than once.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A long-standing demonstrated track record as the person other senior people call when an account is in genuine crisis or&amp;nbsp; gained across a sustained career of Enterprise or Government account ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Credible judgment earned by personally owning the outcomes of dozens of complex enterprise customer account engagements over the course of a career, including situations with real commercial, technical, and reputational stakes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A consistent track record of being trusted by customer executives and internal leadership to operate with minimal oversight in ambiguous and high-pressure situations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep,hands-on expertise in DevSecOps practices, including shift-left security and integrating SAST, DAST, SCA, and container scanning into development workflows as well as architecting and troubleshooting CI/CD pipelines at enterprise scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level understanding of Git, merge request workflows and delivery lifecycles, having personally guided organizations through branching strategies such as trunk-based development and GitFlow, and modern software delivery lifecycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience with infrastructure as code, GitOps, Cloud and on-premises environments with relevant experience that support GitLab deployments, including networking, identity and access management (IAM), secrets management, and deployment considerations for regulated or high-security environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience partnering with customers to turn business requirements into actionable success plans, with measurable goals and verifiable business outcomes that are suitable for executive-level quarterly reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to drive product adoption, dive deep into the accounts assigned and scale out the level of influence in the account.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build and defend executive-level business cases (TCO, compliance, risk) that influence budget and platform strategy decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to operate with autonomy in ambiguous, high-stakes situations with strong communication, stakeholder management, and organizational experience&amp;nbsp; to manage a portfolio of enterprise and Government customers, balance multiple priorities, guide escalations, and coordinate effectively across customer teams and internal cross functional teams to resolve issues appropriately and in a timely manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Customer Success Architect team is part of GitLab&#39;s Customer Experience organization. It supports strategic enterprise and Government accounts across the APJ region through hands-on technical guidance, consultative partnership, and practical problem solving.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We act as a reliable technical advisor and an important link between customers and the broader GitLab ecosystem. We bring platform, cloud, and DevSecOps depth to customer engagements and work closely with Product Management, Engineering, Sales, Support, and Professional Services to address questions, guide customers through technical choices, navigate escalations, and help them realize measurable value from GitLab.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Composed of team members working remotely across time zones, we operate asynchronously to support a focused set of strategic accounts across the region. It&#39;s a team well suited for people who enjoy solving complex customer challenges, building long-term partnerships, and helping enterprise organizations grow their maturity with GitLab in practical, measurable ways.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
