Job Description:
We are looking for a dedicated and enthusiastic Playgroup Leader to deliver and facilitate play opportunities for children in a safe and stimulating environment. The role involves supporting pre-school children in both structured and informal settings, promoting independence, confidence and social interaction.

Key Responsibilities
Supervise children’s games and encourage the development of physical, social and language skills;
Provide play areas and prepare materials for a wide range of children’s activities;
Encourage children’s independence, self-confidence and social interaction;
Organise and supervise children on excursions;
Organise and supervise activities in accordance with Health and Safety regulations, responding appropriately to injuries and emergencies;
Put away equipment and clean premises after use;
Liaise with parents, carers and colleagues, maintaining appropriate records.

Requirements
1–2 years’ experience in early childhood education or recreation roles is desirable;
Strong leadership and organisational skills in managing groups of children;
Passion for working with children, excellent communication and a positive attitude

